{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgHmxotquqChwp1bMVLVg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The form manager now stores each generated identifier on the submission's transaction manager, so a retried save reuses it instead of asking the source for another. The same record also stops an existing patient's identifier from being added twice. I could not find the commit or ticket that introduced this. Falkon has no commit-history tool available to me, and the ticket keys I searched for in the registration app only matched an unrelated test (`O3-5912`).\n\n**What went wrong on retry.** The code comments and test names describe the failure, but I could not read the pre-change code, so this is inferred from them:\n- **New patients:** a retry after a failed patient save called the identifier generator again. Each attempt consumed a new identifier from the source, and the first value was abandoned. The comment at `form-manager.ts:222-223` says the reuse exists \"so a retry does not consume another identifier from the source.\"\n- **Existing patients:** an identifier addition that had already succeeded was repeated on retry, when the later patient save failed. The guard at `form-manager.ts:252-256` skips the addition when the same value was already added in this submission.\n\n**How it is handled now.**\n- `SavePatientTransactionManager` (`form-manager.ts:425-440`) holds `generatedIdentifiers`, keyed by field name with the source UUID, and `addedIdentifiers`, keyed by field name with the value added.\n- `savePatientIdentifiers` (`form-manager.ts:217-235`) reuses the stored value when the source UUID matches. If the source changed, it generates a new one.\n- The `addedIdentifiers` check (`form-manager.ts:252-256`) skips a repeated addition for an existing patient.\n- The component keeps one manager per form instance (`patient-registration.component.tsx:63`, passed at line 94). The test at `patient-registration.test.tsx:681-709` checks that the state survives a re-render for the same patient and resets when the route patient changes.\n\nThe tests at `form-manager.test.ts:724-787` cover each case: the new-patient retry, the existing-patient retry that must not re-add, a failed addition retried with the same value, and a changed source generating a new value.\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-management/packages/esm-patient-registration-app/src/patient-registration/form-manager.ts\", \"startLine\": 217, \"endLine\": 235},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-management/packages/esm-patient-registration-app/src/patient-registration/form-manager.ts\", \"startLine\": 250, \"endLine\": 265},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-management/packages/esm-patient-registration-app/src/patient-registration/form-manager.ts\", \"startLine\": 425, \"endLine\": 440},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-management/packages/esm-patient-registration-app/src/patient-registration/form-manager.test.ts\", \"startLine\": 724, \"endLine\": 787},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-management/packages/esm-patient-registration-app/src/patient-registration/patient-registration.test.tsx\", \"startLine\": 681, \"endLine\": 709},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-management/packages/esm-patient-registration-app/src/patient-registration/patient-registration.component.tsx\", \"startLine\": 63, \"endLine\": 63},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-management/packages/esm-patient-registration-app/src/patient-registration/patient-registration.component.tsx\", \"startLine\": 80, \"endLine\": 95},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-management/packages/esm-patient-registration-app/src/patient-registration/patient-registration.test.tsx\", \"startLine\": 695, \"endLine\": 704},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-management/packages/esm-patient-registration-app/src/patient-registration/form-manager.ts\", \"startLine\": 270, \"endLine\": 275}\n]\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"st